WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:01.840
Zara Larsson, welcome!

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:02.560
Thank you so much!

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:05.640
Zara, the song we just heard, «Like It Is»,

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:09.660
which is a new song, a song you've done with ...

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.260
Kygo and Tyga.

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:12.060
Yes.

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:16.780
The title is «Like It Is», and it is ...

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:22.100
As far as I've understood, it's about what we've spoken about earlier here,

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:24.280
keeping a little distance.

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:26.980
Yes! You could say that.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:31.800
But in the way one has always wanted people to keep their distance,

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:34.520
when they're being intrusive.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:39.460
Yes. It starts like this, «maybe you should leave this girl alone, but you won't».

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:46.300
For me, the song is about a relationship that has ended,

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:51.280
and that this person doesn't understand that, which I ...

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:56.240
I think that everyone has been in that situation, that you're either that person or

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:58.120
you're the one who

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:03.160
just wants this other person to be quiet, maybe.

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:10.860
Or maybe in the club when they approach you, and you're like «I'm not interested, and you don't notice that».

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:12.760
It's like ...

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:17.580
Well, my question is, are men worse at taking hints than women?

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:19.340
Maybe women have

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:23.540
learnt that subconsciously through the years.

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:27.060
And if one were to generalize, I think that

00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:31.240
women are a little better at seeing those small hints.

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:33.440
When has this been tiring for you?

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:39.280
For example, if I don't reply to 15 text messages in a row,

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:41.680
I'm not gonna answer the 16th.

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:44.100
No. And one should get that.

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:45.960
One should get that! Yes.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:50.620
If you're going out, and you're Zara Larsson going out ...

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:52.660
I'm always Zara Larsson.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:55.140
Yes. Yes. And also when you go out.

00:01:55.260 --> 00:02:01.920
And if you're doing what we're not supposed to do now, but before this, going out or things like that ...

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:07.000
Is it harder or easier if the whole world knows that you're single?

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:12.500
If I am to meet someone, it's almost like I'll date someone that I think I'll marry one day.

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:14.300
Even though I'm very young.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:16.080
In what way?

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:19.460
It's like this, I don't really see the point of

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:24.820
seeing someone who I in the future wouldn't see myself ...

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:26.940
I might not marry in the future.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.200
But like, have a future with.

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:33.720
To marry, have children ... Why should I date someone, even though I'm 22,

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:36.580
that I wouldn't want to do that with?

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:38.040
That's how I think.

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:40.460
So I'm very selective with people.

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:44.400
And then when I first meet someone, it goes really fast, and I fall in love.

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:46.200
In one second.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:48.140
And then you imagine the whole future?

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:49.140
Yes.

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:50.740
No.

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:52.380
Or, what?

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:55.200
Well, I was 23 myself ...

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:56.160
It was like that?

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:57.280
Yes, yes, and I had children then.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:00.720
Wow, that's young when you think about it!

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:02.160
I'm 23 soon.

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:04.140
I know that since the last time we spoke ...

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:07.420
I remember, it was a few years ago, you were here ...

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:11.220
We talked about men in groups, and it caused a lot of commotion afterwards.

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:13.220
Because you were quite strict with men in groups.

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:14.340
You generalized.

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:15.280
Yes, I do that.

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:18.080
And people didn't quite understand that you ...

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:19.920
But since then, you've moved.

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:20.920
Yes. I have.

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:21.820
Away from home.

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:24.600
You lived with your mother and father, now you've moved away from home.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:25.820
Yes. Now there's only girls in my apartment.

00:03:25.820 --> 00:03:26.880
Me and my sister.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:30.480
Yes, because your family is still with you, in the form of you sister.

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:31.460
Yes.

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:32.800
Who is the boss there?

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:34.800
I would say that that's my sister.

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:38.280
I tend to call her Miss Goody Two Shoes.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:39.700
She isn't very happy when I say that.

00:03:39.700 --> 00:03:41.360
What does she call you?

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:43.180
Maybe a slob.

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:45.580
Something like that.

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:49.260
But she is fantastic to live with.

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:51.780
She cooks delicious food.

00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:53.820
She cleans really well.

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:59.240
She basically does everything that's needed to keep a household going. And I have to say that

00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:04.080
I will drop to my knees and just praise mom

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:07.120
and dad for doing all these household things.

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:09.280
Because I started to think about

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:13.840
how I've never in my childhood walked on our floors at home

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:17.440
and felt one single crumb under my foot.

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:18.520
It has never happened!

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:20.900
It is so clean in my house!

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:22.340
Very luxurious.

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:25.700
But I haven't understood, until now, how much work that requires.

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:26.320
Exactly!

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:29.140
I'm like, wait, you have to vacuum almost every day!

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:35.040
But there's a theory about people who can stand that it's very messy,

00:04:35.120 --> 00:04:37.120
that they have order on the inside.

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:42.540
While the rest of us, who are tidy on the outside, we're more like chaos ...

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:44.420
Ahhhh, maybe.

00:04:44.420 --> 00:04:46.360
I don't know if that describes me.

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:48.260
Test that with Miss Goody Two Shoes!

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:49.960
I'll do that!

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:54.100
Last time we spoke, you talked about that you

00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:58.700
entrusted control of your economy,

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:02.640
and let's face that the economy in your world is going quite well ...

00:05:02.660 --> 00:05:05.620
Absolutely, I'm doing well. I have no reason to worry.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:08.680
I hope that!

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:11.360
But you mother has control of it.

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:12.520
Yes.

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:14.920
Control and control ...

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:17.640
Well, actually. She does have quite a lot of control.

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:19.440
I have a credit card.

00:05:19.660 --> 00:05:21.880
And with that you can

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:24.660
pay over the internet.

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:26.840
And electronic invoice that I'll get on email.

00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:31.020
And I'll say to her that «I've spent this much».

00:05:31.780 --> 00:05:36.340
Or I'll tell my auditor.

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:41.020
«I have to pay this much this month.»

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:44.620
But mom still wants ... She'll call to get

00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:46.140
the paperwork home.

00:05:46.140 --> 00:05:47.600
To have a look at all expenses.

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:49.240
«What has she spent money on?»

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:50.680
She wants to see what you've spent money on?

00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:52.320
«What have you done for this amount of money?»

00:05:52.360 --> 00:05:55.740
And often, it's a lot of dinners.

00:05:55.740 --> 00:05:58.100
I love treating people I know.

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:02.960
So you treat your friends when you go out?

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:04.220
Absolutely. Yes.

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:06.040
100 percent. It's my favorite thing to do.

00:06:06.040 --> 00:06:07.520
But that's a very expensive life.

00:06:07.720 --> 00:06:09.920
Yes, absolutely. But also ...

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:11.600
I don't know, somewhere ...

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:15.600
Of course, there's not a lot of people my age who have as much money as I do.

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:16.880
At least not my friends.

00:06:16.940 --> 00:06:20.860
Who study or are unemployed right now or

00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:27.680
who have some kind of job and who might not afford to go to this

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:29.920
new restaurant that I want to go to.

00:06:29.920 --> 00:06:32.320
And I don't want to sit there by myself!

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:34.020
With a bag of cash.

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:42.880
Of the things you've bought, what has caused the strongest reaction from your mother?

00:06:45.620 --> 00:06:50.240
There really isn't anything that shocks her, except the fact that I ...

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:54.500
She is very proud. My parents are very proud.

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:56.500
They would never let me pay for anything.

00:06:56.520 --> 00:07:02.280
Even if I'm like, «I know that you want to go on a holiday now. Just say where you want to go, and we'll fix it»!

00:07:02.340 --> 00:07:07.960
«No! No! Dad and I have our own.» They're very proud.

00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:13.260
But then, sometimes when I treat my friends, they'll be like

00:07:13.260 --> 00:07:15.720
«Hah! You never invite me and dad!»

00:07:15.820 --> 00:07:17.820
«But that's because you don't want that.»

00:07:18.020 --> 00:07:22.180
But I enjoy making people happy.

00:07:22.220 --> 00:07:25.460
But I don't think anything shocks her ...

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:28.600
But I actually don't do a lot of crazy things.

00:07:28.700 --> 00:07:32.180
You look at young people who

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:34.780
have become successful

00:07:34.840 --> 00:07:37.000
and have got some money in the bank

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:40.440
and spend them on crazy things.

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:43.120
I wouldn't say that I do that. I have my apartment,

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:45.580
I would love to buy another apartment.

00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:47.500
In L.A.

00:07:47.560 --> 00:07:49.120
Yes, because you've dreamt of moving to L.A.?

00:07:49.120 --> 00:07:50.140
Exactly.

00:07:50.180 --> 00:07:51.260
I want to go there.

00:07:51.260 --> 00:07:53.100
It doesn't look very ..?

00:07:53.100 --> 00:07:55.340
I know! I was going to move in 2020. I thought it would be my year.

00:07:55.760 --> 00:07:56.700
Not so much.

00:07:56.800 --> 00:07:59.240
Have you ever experienced being

00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:04.180
at work, and out traveling, and just felt

00:08:04.180 --> 00:08:07.020
«I have to go home»? «I have to go home to Sweden.»

00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:08.780
Mhm. It's happened once.

00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:10.580
And it was terrible.

00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:11.560
What happened then?

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:14.120
It tends to happen to me at the end of the year.

00:08:14.120 --> 00:08:15.740
I tend to become sick.

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:19.000
Because my body is like «it's over now, I can rest».

00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:20.100
The adrenaline disappears?

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:21.120
Yes, a little like that.

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:25.800
And in that particular moment I was extremely heartbroken as well.

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:28.460
I had a lot of anxiety. I had slept poorly.

00:08:28.460 --> 00:08:30.060
And i just wanted to go home to mom.

00:08:30.640 --> 00:08:31.800
I just wanted to go home to mom.

00:08:31.980 --> 00:08:36.840
So I did something that I had never done before, or after, actually.

00:08:37.220 --> 00:08:40.200
I just said, and it was like a movie,

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:45.580
«You're going to put me on the next flight to Sweden. I'm going home. Tonight.»

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:46.820
«Cancel everything.»

00:08:46.820 --> 00:08:48.360
I had a gig.

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:50.080
I just wanted to go home.

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:53.480
So you were supposed to go on stage?

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:57.100
Not that exact night, but the night after.

00:08:57.340 --> 00:08:58.500
So you cancelled?

00:08:58.500 --> 00:08:59.520
Yes.

00:08:59.820 --> 00:09:02.120
And I'm really not the kind of person to do that.

00:09:02.380 --> 00:09:03.860
But sometimes ...

00:09:03.980 --> 00:09:05.480
But the homesickness took over?

00:09:05.620 --> 00:09:07.620
Yes. And sometimes

00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:09.420
you have to let that happen.

00:09:09.460 --> 00:09:11.940
Better that I then cancelled one gig

00:09:11.960 --> 00:09:13.960
and felt that that was okay.

00:09:14.100 --> 00:09:16.100
It was actually my manager who said

00:09:16.100 --> 00:09:20.800
«If you can't do this, you're allowed to go home.»

00:09:20.820 --> 00:09:24.500
And I've always thought of my career as life and death.

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:25.820
But it isn't.

00:09:25.820 --> 00:09:26.980
It's my life, actually.

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:29.740
And if I'm feeling shitty in a situation,

00:09:30.340 --> 00:09:34.440
I think that my priority should be to not feel like shit.

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:36.300
In those moments, pop music is just pop music?

00:09:36.340 --> 00:09:39.080
It's like that. So then I went home to mommy.

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:42.000
Zara, it's wonderful to have you back.

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:42.920
It's good to be here!

00:09:42.920 --> 00:09:44.620
We're having another guest on.

00:09:45.200 --> 00:09:46.120
Bring'em in!

